PianoWifi is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). Level 1 only: a read-only survey. What it takes from other
work, and from where:

UniXNU-sheng (unixnu-research/UniXNU-sheng, main 00ba90984e831e4c6ce30ec3d8a56e6434e9f1af), BSD-2-Clause-Patent (LICENSE sha256
5b1d3d911103cb0f41641ec0964c5ac1f7e229f57aa072b6ac38bae913a1307b; SM8550 + WCN7850, the Wi-Fi path hardware-verified there per its
porting.toml), package/WifiProbe.cpp (sha256 72f46e8229865eff68feae9a3002b919ad3b610e634d93877879f4960d5b01a0):
  Design only, re-implemented (no code copied): a level that only looks before any level powers anything; the controller's
  registers read only when its power domain is on and its interface clocks run ("a read of an unclocked block stalls the bus");
  the TLMM pin layout (also used by PianoPower and PianoDwc3); the SMPS peripheral page rule 0x9b + 3 * (n - 1). Its SM8550
  addresses (DBI 0x60000000, GCC branch offsets, the v6 PHY layout) are NOT piano's and are not used.

UniXNU-Pagani-Drivers (github.com/Shad0w23333/UniXNU-Pagani-Drivers 3d570b7653bf9831def8fe49b339b42990508d83, also
IssacL04/UniXNU-Pagani-Drivers), drivers/PaganiWifi, BSD-2-Clause-Patent (LICENSE sha256 as UniXNU-sheng's; SM8750 + the same
17cb:110e chip on the OnePlus 13T; host-tested only, never run on a device), PaganiWifiTables.h (sha256
001f808ba5dd4356b1e31efcfd9631c0a1064d71201c29f73cf55f3efb859516), WifiBringup.cpp (sha256
bb40a62361e06870348cd66eecca0634fb0e48d36a60afcb3f3acb0035ab3cd2):
  Facts only, cross-checked against mainline Linux (below) where mainline has them: the SM8750 PCIe0 GDSC, collapse vote, branch
  CBCR / vote bit / hardware-gating table, BCRs, RCGs and pipe mux; the v7 PHY layout; the LDO page rule 0xc0 + n on SM8750's
  PMICs (its running DT's OCP notifier names); the PMK8550 gpio3 sleep clock pin; gpio19 / 202 / 203; the cmd-db names of the
  supplies and the PCIe NoC BCM (SN4). Board values of the 13T (its rails, PPIDs, PHY sequence) are not piano's and are not used.

